                     <title>Augustinus, De verbis domini</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The verses recorded by Young (no. 18) "Christe
                        tui calicis predo sit preda Kalucis | Ere breui reicis qui tulit era crucis"
                        are on fol. 184r.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Several names in a memorandum at end, s.
                        xv/xvi. One of them, Norman Wasporn, is presumably the Norman Wassheburn to
                        whom Prior Wm. More made a payment recorded in his diary (W.H.S.
                        233).</note>
